From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sophgo: cv1800: clear the cam0_200 crystal bypass

TRM 8.9.7: clk_byp_0 bit 16 is the clock bypass to xtal for clk_cam0_200
and its reset value is 1. The bootloader leaves it set, so every UART
(clk_uart0..4 derive from clk_cam0_200) runs from the 25 MHz crystal and
base_baud stays 1,562,500 - the modem 2 Mbaud cannot be set.

div_clk_cam0_200 (TRM 8.9.27) already selects disppll with divider 1,
so clearing the bypass is enough. This only touches a mux register; no
PLL is reprogrammed.

The pr_info lines are diagnostic: they show the register before and after
the clear and the rates the clock framework derives from them.

--- a/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv1800.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sophgo/clk-cv1800.c
@@ -1509,6 +1509,18 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(reg))
 		return PTR_ERR(reg);
 
+	/*
+	 * clk_byp_0 bit 16 forces clk_cam0_200 (the UART baud clock) to the
+	 * 25 MHz crystal. The bootloader leaves it set; div_clk_cam0_200
+	 * already selects disppll, so clearing it is enough for 2 Mbaud.
+	 * Register access only: no PLL is reprogrammed.
+	 */
+	pr_info("rnsbox-clk pre: byp=0x%08x div=0x%08x%c",
+		readl(reg + REG_CLK_BYP_0), readl(reg + REG_DIV_CLK_CAM0_200), 10);
+	if (readl(reg + REG_CLK_BYP_0) & BIT(16))
+		writel(readl(reg + REG_CLK_BYP_0) & ~BIT(16), reg + REG_CLK_BYP_0);
+	pr_info("rnsbox-clk post: byp=0x%08x%c", readl(reg + REG_CLK_BYP_0), 10);
+
 	desc = device_get_match_data(dev);
 	if (!desc) {
 		dev_err(dev, "no match data for platform\n");
@@ -1525,7 +1537,12 @@
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	return cv1800_clk_init_ctrl(dev, reg, ctrl, desc);
+	ret = cv1800_clk_init_ctrl(dev, reg, ctrl, desc);
+	if (!ret)
+		pr_info("rnsbox-clk rates: cam0_200=%lu disppll=%lu%c",
+			clk_hw_get_rate(&clk_cam0_200.mux.common.hw),
+			clk_hw_get_rate(&clk_disppll.common.hw), 10);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id cv1800_clk_ids[] = {

